Summary: Retry write faults on pages mapped both writable and executable
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover (ported here)
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 24945
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
  Note: CX 26.3.0's form differs from 25.1.1's only in putting the done:
    label under #ifdef __APPLE__. Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: ntdll.so:
    "HACK: write fault on a w|x page, addr %p"
  Changes: retries only if the page's Mach protection includes write after
    the toggle; otherwise the fault goes on to Wine's normal handling (CX
    retries regardless, and loops for ever if the mprotect didn't take);
    CW HACK 25719, next to it in CX 26.3.0 (the same toggle for an exec
    fault on an executable page), isn't taken: Sikarugir 10.0_8 doesn't
    have it
Upstream: no
Why: Under Rosetta 2 a write fault can hit a page that is mapped both
 writable and executable (presumably Rosetta write-protecting a page whose
 code it has translated), and Wine, which doesn't expect a write fault on
 a writable page, raises an access violation. On macOS, drop and re-add
 exec on the page and retry the write instead. The retry happens only if
 the page is writable at the Mach level afterwards, so a page whose
 protection Wine can't change doesn't fault the same write for ever.
Programs: none known
Fine on: macOS 26.7.2 (M1 Max): the hack never fires in smc-rwx or in a
 version with a second thread calling the code (10.0 build0, 11.22 quick
 build, WINEDEBUG=fixme+virtual)
Messages: "HACK: write fault on a w|x page, addr %p" (fixme:virtual; shown
 by default); "page %p still isn't writable, not retrying" (warn:virtual;
 shown only with WINEDEBUG=warn+virtual)
Uncertain: when Rosetta lets such a fault through. Whether smc-rwx guards
 this patch: on macOS 26.7.2 it passes without the hack firing, and its
 failure on plain Wine on macOS 15 may be the wow64 mode-switch crash
 that wow64cpu-rosetta-lretq works around (WineHQ bugs 60034, 60494). The
 guard catches a toggle that doesn't make the page writable; if Rosetta
 went on faulting a page that is writable, the write would still be
 retried for ever. A plain retry-once (same address twice from one
 thread) can't be used: a program that rewrites and runs the same code in
 a loop (tests/regress/smc-rwx) faults at the same address and
 instruction every round, legitimately.
Status: 11.21: 2026-11-26: retries only if the page is writable after the
 toggle
 11.22: 2026-11-26: retries only if the page is writable after the
 toggle
 11.21: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T005336 and T023339 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed
 11.22: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T002454 and T025644 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -4414,7 +4414,25 @@ static NTSTATUS grow_thread_stack( struct thread_data 
     else data->teb->Tib.StackLimit = page;
     return ret;
 }
+
+
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+/* whether the host page is writable at the Mach level (CW Hack 24945's retry) */
+static BOOL wx_page_writable( void *page )
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t address = (mach_vm_address_t)page;
+    mach_vm_size_t size = 0;
+    vm_region_basic_info_data_64_t info;
+    mach_msg_type_number_t count = VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_COUNT_64;
+    mach_port_t object_name;
 
+    if (mach_vm_region( mach_task_self(), &address, &size, VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_64,
+                        (vm_region_info_t)&info, &count, &object_name ))
+        return TRUE;  /* can't tell: retry, as before */
+    if (address > (mach_vm_address_t)page) return TRUE;
+    return (info.protection & VM_PROT_WRITE) != 0;
+}
+#endif
 
 /***********************************************************************
  *           virtual_handle_fault
@@ -4437,6 +4455,25 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_handle_fault( struct thread_data *dat
         WARN( "treating read fault in a readable page as a write fault, addr %p\n", addr );
         err = EXCEPTION_WRITE_FAULT;
     }
+
+    /* CW Hack 24945 */
+    if (err == EXCEPTION_WRITE_FAULT &&
+        ((get_unix_prot( vprot ) & (PROT_WRITE | PROT_EXEC)) == (PROT_WRITE | PROT_EXEC)))
+    {
+        FIXME( "HACK: write fault on a w|x page, addr %p\n", addr );
+        mprotect_range( page, page_size, 0, VPROT_EXEC );
+        mprotect_range( page, page_size, VPROT_EXEC, 0 );
+        /* wine-mac-builds: retry only if the page really is writable now.
+         * If the mprotect didn't take (the mapping's maximum protection has
+         * no write, say), the retried write would fault the same way for
+         * ever; let the fault take its normal course instead. */
+        if (wx_page_writable( page ))
+        {
+            ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+            goto done;
+        }
+        WARN( "page %p still isn't writable, not retrying\n", page );
+    }
 #endif
 
     if (!is_inside_signal_stack( data, stack ) && (vprot & VPROT_GUARD))
@@ -4473,6 +4510,10 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_handle_fault( struct thread_data *dat
                 ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
         }
     }
+
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+done:
+#endif
     mutex_unlock( &virtual_mutex );
     rec->ExceptionCode = ret;
     return ret;
